    <!-- Permission rationales shown in Play Console listings -->
    <string name="perm_camera_rationale">Take photos of squawks and completed work so admins can verify repairs.</string>
    <string name="perm_photos_rationale">Attach existing photos to squawks and work logs.</string>
    <string name="perm_notifications_rationale">Get alerts when squawks are filed, work is assigned, or parts arrive.</string>

    <!--
      TRANSLATION RULE — regulatory and trade terms stay in English.

      Squawk, AD (airworthiness directive), RTS (return to service), A&P, IA,
      AOG, AMM, IPC, SRM, T&E, N-number, logbook and "core" (the old unit
      returned to the vendor for credit) are NOT translated in any locale. Non-English shops use the English terms because the manuals, the
      logbook entries and the regulator use them; translating "squawk" into
      six languages would invent six words nobody in a hangar says, and a
      mistranslated airworthiness term in a maintenance record is a safety
      problem, not a UX one.

      Everything else — verbs, navigation, status, buttons, help text — is
      translated normally.
    -->

